# Portable Critic Setup

A lightweight, container-agnostic critic pack for validating agent JSON outputs and generating review artifacts. Run it inside your container to sanity-check and audit outputs.

---

## Contents

```
critic_setup/
├─ critic_legacy.py
├─ validate_output.py
├─ validate_json_min.py
├─ fix_json.py
├─ gemini_audit.py
├─ critic_output.json          # sample JSON (default input)
├─ schema_output.json          # JSON Schema used by validators
└─ README
```

Scripts overview:

* critic_legacy.py – runs the legacy critic suite.
* validate_output.py – schema and content checks.
* validate_json_min.py – minimal sanity check (no external deps).
* fix_json.py – repairs formatting and renames legacy keys.
* gemini_audit.py – LLM-based expert-style audit.

---

## Wrapper Output Contract

The wrapper must emit a JSON file (critic_output.json by default):

```json
[
  {
    "id": "unique-id",
    "task": "short description",
    "model": "model name",
    "prompt": "input prompt",
    "response": "LLM output",
    "metadata": { "extra": "allowed" }
  }
]
```

Extra keys are allowed; validators ignore unknown fields.

---

## Quick Start

Run inside the critic_setup directory:

```bash
cd critic_setup

# 1. Minimal check
python validate_json_min.py critic_output.json

# 2. Auto-fix common issues
python fix_json.py critic_output.json critic_output.fixed.json
python validate_json_min.py critic_output.fixed.json

# 3. Full validation
python validate_output.py critic_output.json

# 4. Critic
python critic_legacy.py critic_output.json

# 5. Audit report
python gemini_audit.py critic_output.json --out ./out/audit/critic_report.txt
```

Artifacts go to ./out/.

---

## Docker Usage

### Option A – Copy folder into image

```dockerfile
COPY critic_setup /app/critic_setup
WORKDIR /app/critic_setup
```

### Option B – Mount at runtime (recommended)

```bash
docker run --rm -it \
  -v $(pwd)/critic_setup:/app/critic_setup \
  -v $(pwd)/your-wrapper-out:/app/wrapper_out \
  -w /app/critic_setup \
  your_image_name \
  bash -lc "python validate_json_min.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python validate_output.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python critic_legacy.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python gemini_audit.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json --out ./out/audit/critic_report.txt"
```

---

## Makefile (optional)

```make
CRITIC_DIR ?= critic_setup
WRAP_OUT ?= your-wrapper-out/critic_output.json
PY ?= python

quick:
	$(PY) $(CRITIC_DIR)/validate_json_min.py $(WRAP_OUT)

validate:
	$(PY) $(CRITIC_DIR)/validate_output.py $(WRAP_OUT)

critic:
	$(PY) $(CRITIC_DIR)/critic_legacy.py $(WRAP_OUT)

audit:
	$(PY) $(CRITIC_DIR)/gemini_audit.py $(WRAP_OUT) --out $(CRITIC_DIR)/out/audit/critic_report.txt

fix:
	$(PY) $(CRITIC_DIR)/fix_json.py $(WRAP_OUT) $(CRITIC_DIR)/critic_output.fixed.json
```

Run with:

```bash
make quick
make validate
make critic
make audit
```

---

## Runner Image (if no Python in container)

```bash
docker run --rm -it \
  -v $(pwd)/critic_setup:/app/critic_setup \
  -v $(pwd)/your-wrapper-out:/app/wrapper_out \
  -w /app/critic_setup \
  python:3.11-slim \
  bash -lc "pip install -r requirements.txt || true; \
            python validate_json_min.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python validate_output.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python critic_legacy.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json && \
            python gemini_audit.py /app/wrapper_out/critic_output.json --out ./out/audit/critic_report.txt"
```

---

## CLI Help

```bash
python validate_json_min.py --help
python validate_output.py --help
python critic_legacy.py --help
python gemini_audit.py --help
python fix_json.py --help
```

Common flags:

* --input <path> – JSON file path (default: critic_output.json)
* --outdir <dir> – output directory
* --strict – strict mode (when available)

---

## Team Workflow

1. Each member keeps their own container.
2. Copy or mount critic_setup inside.
3. Wrapper writes critic_output.json.
4. Run: quick → validate → critic → audit.
5. Share out/ artifacts.

